! mcp_bootstrap_p48.strap -- RESERVATIONS, TABLES AND COUNTERS, the
! DECODE program's storage, printed page 48.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.55, header "PAGE NUMBER 48".
! docs/boot_plan.md M3.
!
! >>> PRINTED p.47 COMPILES NOTHING, so this page follows printed
! p.46 directly. <<<
!
! p.47 is twenty-three lines and the only one that is not a comment
! is line 1's "SLC,$" at 002556.67 -- which is where printed p.46's
! Q BLNK ends, to the bit.  The rest of it is THE DECODE PROGRAM
! LINKAGE FORMAT, written out as a worked call:
!
!         LVI,$15,X
!         B,LDECOD
!   X     VF,A          LET A = FWA OF THE BREAK DOWN AREA
!         CF,B          LET B = THE MODE
!                         ZERO = OVERLAP MODE
!                         NOT ZERO = NOT OVERLAP MODE
!         VF,C          LET C = THE RETURN DISPOSITIONS
!         BEW,$   ERROR RETURN
!         BEW,$   NORMAL RETURN
!                       SEE THE DISTRIBUTED WRITE - UP
!
! -- so DECODE is handed the area printed pp.45-46's S BRK8 filled.
! That is recorded in docs/boot_plan.md; there is no deck for p.47
! because there is nothing to compile and nothing to check.
!
! AND THIS PAGE OPENS A FIFTH SOURCE DECK: the card sequence is
! 16000001, where printed pp.42-46 were 15000xxx.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE BIT CHAIN AT THE END IS A SECOND WITNESS FOR VF = 25 BITS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 44 is "L NO6  VF,.06" at 002601.00 and line 45 is at
! 002601.31 -- BIT 25.  printed p.46 lines 29-30 forced that
! correction (C22-6531 printed p.18, "THE LOCATION COUNTER STANDS AT
! BIT 25") and this page confirms it independently, then chains
! eight more rows off it without a single byte boundary:
!
!   .31 + 7  = .40   line 45's DRZ(BU,7)
!   .40 + 9  = .51   line 46's DRZ(BU,9)
!   .51 + 1  = .52   line 47's DD(BU,1)
!   .52 + 1  = .53   line 48's DD(BU,1)
!   .53 + 7  = .62   line 49's DRZ(BU,7)
!   .62 + 1  = .63   line 50's DD(BU,1)
!   .63 + 8  = .73   line 51's (AX)DD(BU,8,8)
!
! Every one of those addresses is printed, so the chain is checked
! end to end rather than asserted.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EIGHT MORE INDEX-REGISTER SYNs
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 33-40 are "L IODX SYN,$3" through "L WORKX SYN,$10" -- the
! shape printed p.46 lines 22-24 introduced and strap_asm.py was
! taught on the same day (C22-6531 printed p.31: "THE MEANING OF SYN
! IS ALWAYS ONE OF EXACT SUBSTITUTION").  The listing prints their
! LOCATION as the register's own bit address, 000023.00 through
! 000032.00, which is what this deck checks.
!
! AND LINE 5 IS THE SAME PSEUDO-OP CARRYING BOTH A dds AND A BIT
! ADDRESS: "L IREF  SYN(BU,12),0.52".  The listing prints the
! location 000000.64 -- 0o64 is 52 -- so the "52" is DECIMAL in the
! source and OCTAL in the location column, which is this listing's
! habit everywhere.  The dds column prints "BU,14 ,10", octal for
! (BU,12,8).
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! SUBSTITUTIONS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) BLANKS INSIDE SYMBOL NAMES ARE DROPPED, as on every page since
!     p.2.  Note that three names on this page are printed with NO
!     blank -- LPPREF, LIOTBX and LFSTRX -- beside eleven that have
!     one.
!
! (2) LINE 1'S "PRNS" IS WRITTEN AS PRINTED and discarded
!     (LISTING_CONTROL); it is print control and emits nothing.
!
! (3) NOTHING ELSE.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LINE 50'S NAME IS "L OVBIT" AND THIS DECK READ IT "L CVBIT",
! which printed p.52 corrected the same day.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! p.52 line 11 is "BB1,L OVBIT,L OVER" and its binary carries the
! address 002601.62 -- THIS ROW.  A second print of the same symbol,
! three pages on, in a listing whose drum turns digit zeros into Cs:
! that is listing_typography.md 13c's rule ("decode what a name
! labels") in its cheapest form, because a NAME field has no
! internal check and a REFERENCE to it does.
!
! The comment on this row said so too -- "-OVERLAPPED JOB", and
! OVBIT is the OVerlap BIT -- which is the tell that was there to be
! read and was not.
!
! NO COMPILED BIT MOVED.  The symbol is unreferenced within this
! page, so the rename changes the symbol table and nothing else; it
! is the IMAGE that would have broken, silently, the first time p.52
! joined it and resolved L OVBIT to nothing.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LINE 46 IS A ROW WHERE THE DRUM LOST SEVERAL GLYPHS AT ONCE,
! which is listing_typography.md 13d's shape.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! At 900 dpi it prints
!
!     L ICSCR  DRZ(BU,9),(1)        -ICDSQ COLNTER
!
! and "COLNTER" is "COUNTER", so at least one glyph on the row is
! wrong before anything else is read.  The NAME is transcribed
! "L IOSCR" and the comment "-IODSQ COUNTER".
!
! WHAT MAKES THAT SAFE RATHER THAN A GUESS: the symbol is not
! referenced anywhere on this page, so NO COMPILED BIT DEPENDS ON
! ITS SPELLING -- only the reservation's nine bits do, and those are
! checked by line 47's address.  The reading itself leans on line
! 35, "L XIO  SYN,$5  -I.O. REQUEST TABLE INDEX", which is this
! program writing I-O as "IO" in a name on the same page.  IF A
! LATER PAGE REFERENCES THIS SYMBOL, that print is the decider and
! this note is the thing to come back to.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE SIXTEEN STAND-INS, read off this page's own binary
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   T PURFT 003370.00  T UPPC  2      lines 9 and 23's value/count
!   T UIORQ 003514.00  T UIOC  20     line 10
!   T UFRE  003623.00  T UFRC  20     line 11
!   T PREFT 003317.00  T PPC   20     lines 12 and 23
!   T IOREQ 003373.00  T IOC   80     lines 13 and 24
!   T FSTRE 003541.00  T FRC   50     lines 14 and 25
!   L SYMU  002620.00                 lines 15 and 26
!   L SYMC  002660.00                 lines 16 and 27
!   L NTPU  002700.00                 lines 17 and 28
!   L DISK  002723.00                 line 18
!
! THE COUNTS ARE INTEGERS, NOT ADDRESSES, and the listing's own
! arithmetic says so: lines 15-17 write "32-2" and "16-2" where the
! count column prints 000036 and 000016 -- 30 and 14 in octal -- so
! a count is a plain number and the deck SYNs these as integers.

        SLC, (8)2557.0

TPURFT  SYN, (8)3370.0
TUPPC   SYN, 2
TUIORQ  SYN, (8)3514.0
TUIOC   SYN, 20
TUFRE   SYN, (8)3623.0
TUFRC   SYN, 20
TPREFT  SYN, (8)3317.0
TPPC    SYN, 20
TIOREQ  SYN, (8)3373.0
TIOC    SYN, 80
TFSTRE  SYN, (8)3541.0
TFRC    SYN, 50
LSYMU   SYN, (8)2620.0
LSYMC   SYN, (8)2660.0
LNTPU   SYN, (8)2700.0
LDISK   SYN, (8)2723.0

        PRNS                        ! line 1

! ---- RESERVATIONS, TABLES AND COUNTERS -----------------------------
LIREF   SYN(BU,12), 0.52            ! line 5  -P.P. REFERENCE NUMBER

        SLC, (8)2557.0

! ---- TABLE INDICES FOR REFILL USE ----------------------------------
LPPURF  XW, TPURFT, TUPPC, $        ! line 9  -NOT OVERLAP PP REF.
        XW, TUIORQ, TUIOC, $        ! line 10 -NOT OVERLAP I/O REQ.
        XW, TUFRE, TUFRC, $         ! line 11 -NOT OVERLAP FIRST REEL
LPPREF  XW, TPREFT, TPPC, $         ! line 12
LIOTBX  XW, TIOREQ, TIOC, $         ! line 13
LFSTRX  XW, TFSTRE, TFRC, $         ! line 14
LSYMUX  XW, LSYMU, 32-2, $          ! line 15 -SYMBOLIC TAPE INDEX
LSYMCX  XW, LSYMC, 16-2, $          ! line 16 -SYMBOLIC CHANNEL INDEX
LNTPUX  XW, LNTPU, 16-2, $          ! line 17 -NON-TAPE INDEX REFILL
LXTYPE  XW, LDISK, 9, $             ! line 18 -THE TYPE CODE INDEX

! ---- SWAP AREA FOR EIGHT MCP-DECODE INDICES ------------------------
LTY     XW                          ! line 22
        XW, TPREFT, TPPC, LPPREF    ! line 23
        XW, TIOREQ, TIOC, LIOTBX    ! line 24
        XW, TFSTRE, TFRC, LFSTRX    ! line 25
        XW, LSYMU, 32-2, LSYMUX     ! line 26
        XW, LSYMC, 16-2, LSYMCX     ! line 27
        XW, LNTPU, 16-2, LNTPUX     ! line 28
        XW                          ! line 29

! ---- TABLE INDICES -------------------------------------------------
LIODX   SYN, $3                     ! line 33 -INDEX FOR GETTING IOD
                                     !           IMAGE
LXPP    SYN, $4                     ! line 34 -P.P. REFERENCE TABLE
                                     !           INDEX
LXIO    SYN, $5                     ! line 35 -I.O. REQUEST TABLE
                                     !           INDEX
LXFR    SYN, $6                     ! line 36 -FIRST REEL NUMBER
                                     !           TABLE INDEX
LXSU    SYN, $7                     ! line 37 -SYMBOLIC TAPE UNIT
                                     !           TABLE INDEX
LXSC    SYN, $8                     ! line 38 -SYMBOLIC CHANNEL TABLE
                                     !           INDEX
LXNT    SYN, $9                     ! line 39 -NON-TAPE TABLE INDEX
LWORKX  SYN, $10                    ! line 40 -WORKING INDEX

! ---- COUNTERS AND BITS ---------------------------------------------
LNO6    VF, .06                     ! line 44 -FOR IX BUMMPING (sic)
LTAPEC  DRZ(BU,7), (1)              ! line 45 -TAPE REEL COUNTER
LIOSCR  DRZ(BU,9), (1)              ! line 46 -IODSQ COUNTER; see the
                                     !           note above
LFINB   DD(BU,1), 1                 ! line 47 -FINAL BIT
LNTB    DD(BU,1), 0                 ! line 48 -NON-TAPE BIT
LCOUNT  DRZ(BU,7), (1)              ! line 49 -COUNT OF RLSYMS
LOVBIT  DD(BU,1), 0                 ! line 50 -OVERLAPPED JOB
LBLZOR  (AX)DD(BU,8,8),0X           ! line 51 -BCD -8 ZERO
LINFAD  DD(BU,1), 0                 ! line 52 -INFINITE-DISK A...

        END, LPPURF

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! AND TWO LISTING MARKS, the bare "*" after the location that every
! page since printed p.3 carries: lines 23 ("002572.00 *") and 45
! ("002601.31 *").
